			<div class="content" id="post-content-924378">
									

<blockquote>
<p>Changes undergone by 333-α appear to constitute the inclusion of motifs representing any foreign materials left behind by exploration teams. Given that copies of original 333-α do not update to reflect material within 333-β, it may be possible to selectively manifest materials and possibly even personnel within 333-β. A more in-depth cost-benefit analysis will follow.</p>
</blockquote>
<p>This here is the exact paragraph that got me to hit the upvote button. Nice work.</p>
<p>Edit: Although I should also mention that I kinda grit my teeth when a nuke was involved during testing. The monster doesn't need to be so tough to survive a nuke to be scary. I'd personally like it a lot better if they set off a nuke inside the city and then all the musical scores were retroactively changed to horrible noise because of the destruction left behind.</p>

							</div>

								
